.TH GOBAN-ENFORCER 8 "August 2026" "GoBan" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
goban-enforcer \- minimal privileged firewall helper for GoBan
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B goban-enforcer
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B goban-enforcer
owns GoBan's firewall capabilities in privilege-separated deployments. It
listens on a private Unix socket and accepts only typed setup, policy-reload,
ban, unban, list, diagnostics, and close operations from the configured daemon
UID (or root). It does not parse logs, load rule expressions, expose the operator
control API, or accept arbitrary firewall commands.
.PP
Packaged systemd installations run
.B goban-daemon
as the unprivileged goban user and start this helper automatically as the
separate non-login goban-enforcer user. The helper refuses normal startup unless
its runtime privilege state is non-root, NoNewPrivileges is enabled, and its
effective, bounding, and ambient capability masks contain only CAP_NET_ADMIN.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " path"
GoBan YAML configuration. Default: /etc/goban/goban.yaml.
.TP
.BI --rules-dir " path"
Optional rules directory used while validating effective configuration.
.TP
.BI --socket " path"
Override the private enforcer Unix socket.
.TP
.BI --allowed-user " user"
Override the Unix user permitted to connect.
.TP
.B --version
Print the build version and exit.
.SH SECURITY
The socket is forced to mode 0660 between the separate helper and detector identities.
The server also validates Linux SO_PEERCRED on every accepted Unix connection.
No protocol operation can carry a shell command or firewall expression. Request
bodies, headers, connection concurrency, IP/rule/TTL values, and protocol version
are bounded or validated. The helper independently refuses loopback, multicast,
local-interface, global-allowlist, and per-rule-allowlist ban targets. On hot
reload it independently reloads the root-managed policy and swaps it only when
its semantic fingerprint matches the detector's expected fingerprint.
.PP
The packaged unit runs the helper as the separate non-login goban-enforcer user
and bounds it to CAP_NET_ADMIN only. The helper primary group is goban so the
detector can open the socket; SO_PEERCRED still admits only the configured
detector UID (or root).
A compromised detector can still request typed bans of non-protected remote
addresses or typed unbans; the split limits kernel/root capability rather than
proving detector intent.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR goban-daemon (8),
.BR goban-client (1)
